           Question
In response to the latest tool implementation at xFusionCorp Industries, the system admins require the creation of a service user account. Here are the specifics:
Create a user named james in App Server 3 without a home directory.
Note: You can find the infrastructure details by clicking on the Details of all Users and Servers button on the top-right section of the page.

           Solution
1-Login App server 3
   ssh banner@stapp03
2-Create a new user without a home directory
   sudo useradd --no-create-home james
.  --no-create-home ensures no home directory is created.
. By default, the shell will be /bin/bash unless specified otherwise.
3-(Optional) Assign a non-interactive shell if required
.If this service account should not allow logins:
   sudo usermod -s /sbin/nologin james
4-Validate the user creation
.Check user details:
   id james
   getent passwd james
.Confirm no home directory exists:
   ls -ld /home/james
This should return No such file or directory
